# Tshepong Mining Incentive System — environment overrides
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and uncomment/edit whichever lines you need.
# ".env" is gitignored on purpose — real server credentials should never be committed.
#
# Leave everything commented out to keep using the defaults in config/config.yaml
# (local dev: Windows-authenticated connection to localhost\MSSQLSERVER01).
#
# To point this app at a different SQL Server (e.g. the Harmony server), uncomment
# DB_SERVER below and, if that server needs SQL login rather than Windows auth,
# also uncomment DB_USERNAME and DB_PASSWORD. Setting DB_USERNAME is what switches
# the app from Windows Trusted Connection to SQL Server authentication — see
# config/settings.py -> DatabaseSettings.build_connection_string().

# Hostname\instance of the SQL Server to connect to.
# Examples: HARMONYSQL01  or  HARMONYSQL01\INSTANCENAME
#DB_SERVER=harmony-server-hostname

# Only needed if the target server requires SQL Server authentication instead of
# Windows auth (i.e. logging in with a SQL username/password rather than your
# Windows domain account). Leave both commented out to use Windows auth.
#DB_USERNAME=your-sql-username
#DB_PASSWORD=your-sql-password

# Only needed if the database name differs from STPTM4000 on the target server.
#DB_DATABASE=STPTM4000
